    ($SATQ$42b4493b$SATQ$, $SATQ$2b0e8838-4d1b-4eaf-9a92-439aa05ee874$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a3013429-5120-4766-9128-9404ef045e8d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">In a right triangle, the measure of one of the acute angles is <math alttext="51 degree"><mrow><mn>51</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the measure, in degrees, of the other acute angle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e2e1aa8b-8de3-4cfe-8c02-10371a8a6ab2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0ebf5c98-c2f4-4ec3-a685-af6fbbea58d7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"15c72fd8-ce26-4352-975f-ee5f7165a29d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c38d0f92-ec62-41ef-803b-b316310ef964","content":"<p><math alttext=\"51\"><mn>51</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0ebf5c98-c2f4-4ec3-a685-af6fbbea58d7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext="180"><mn>180</mn>
</math> degrees. Since the triangle is a right triangle, it has one angle that measures <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math> degrees. Therefore, the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the remaining two angles is <math alttext="180 minus 90"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn></math>, or <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of one of the acute angles in the triangle is <math alttext="51"><mn>51</mn>
</math> degrees. Therefore, the measure, in degrees, of the other acute angle is <math alttext="90 minus 51"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>51</mn></math>, or <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the acute angle whose measure is given.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"42b4493b","external_id":"2b0e8838-4d1b-4eaf-9a92-439aa05ee874","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"a3013429-5120-4766-9128-9404ef045e8d","uId":"e3c0454d-db7f-4b1a-be39-c12164fc3943","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In a right triangle, the measure of one of the acute angles is <math alttext=\"51 degree\"><mrow><mn>51</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the measure, in degrees, of the other acute angle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e2e1aa8b-8de3-4cfe-8c02-10371a8a6ab2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0ebf5c98-c2f4-4ec3-a685-af6fbbea58d7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"15c72fd8-ce26-4352-975f-ee5f7165a29d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"49\"><mn>49</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c38d0f92-ec62-41ef-803b-b316310ef964","content":"<p><math alttext=\"51\"><mn>51</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["0ebf5c98-c2f4-4ec3-a685-af6fbbea58d7"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math> degrees. Since the triangle is a right triangle, it has one angle that measures <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> degrees. Therefore, the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the remaining two angles is <math alttext=\"180 minus 90\"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of one of the acute angles in the triangle is <math alttext=\"51\"><mn>51</mn>\n</math> degrees. Therefore, the measure, in degrees, of the other acute angle is <math alttext=\"90 minus 51\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>51</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the acute angle whose measure is given.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959838,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"42b4493b","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959838,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"2b0e8838-4d1b-4eaf-9a92-439aa05ee874","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"e3c0454d-db7f-4b1a-be39-c12164fc3943","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["0ebf5c98-c2f4-4ec3-a685-af6fbbea58d7"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math> degrees. Since the triangle is a right triangle, it has one angle that measures <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math> degrees. Therefore, the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the remaining two angles is <math alttext=\"180 minus 90\"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>90</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of one of the acute angles in the triangle is <math alttext=\"51\"><mn>51</mn>\n</math> degrees. Therefore, the measure, in degrees, of the other acute angle is <math alttext=\"90 minus 51\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>51</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from concept