<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for diagram of 3 lines" class="sr-only"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled k, m, and n.</li>
<li>Line k intersects both line m and line n.</li>
<li>At the intersection of line k and line n, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>
<ul>
<li>Top left: x°</li>
<li>Bottom right: 145°</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the figure, line <math alttext="m"><mi>m</mi>
</math> is parallel to line <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math>, and line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> intersects both lines. Which of the following statements is true?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4e3d63cb-23b3-4103-8cb1-829746a08a54","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is less than <math alttext=\"145\"><mn>145</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"ffd77068-fbf4-42f4-bc7a-21a59cbe8f96","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"145\"><mn>145</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"b7f584a8-7c1d-448a-849d-07bd460b7376","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is equal to <math alttext=\"145\"><mn>145</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"1663fa11-75f0-4035-be94-fcb210e0f135","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> cannot be determined.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["b7f584a8-7c1d-448a-849d-07bd460b7376"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. Vertical angles, or angles that are opposite each other when two lines intersect, are congruent. It&rsquo;s given that line <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> intersects line <math alttext="n"><mi>n</mi>
</math>. Based on the figure, the angle with measure <math alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle with measure <math alttext="145 degree"><mn>145</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is equal to <math alttext="145"><mn>145</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
