    ($SATQ$4420e500$SATQ$, $SATQ$76f07394-0a95-4e65-86b8-e42618d65c92$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$096e7ca7-535a-43c1-a773-3edf7dfda31a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>What is the area of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext="4 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> and a width of <math alttext="2 cm"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"360cb884-e056-4da9-b845-1b2f1b6ae601","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 cm squared\"><mn>6</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"9eea382e-cf7d-42ac-b0a9-bc63f318fb27","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8 cm squared\"><mn>8</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"ffb279aa-4624-4600-97e3-111747624f24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12 cm squared\"><mn>12</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"9db1eaef-eb78-4768-b1b5-95d9fd91895f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36 cm squared\"><mn>36</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9eea382e-cf7d-42ac-b0a9-bc63f318fb27"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The area of a rectangle with length <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and width <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> can be found using the formula <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext="4 cm"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>&nbsp;and a width of&nbsp;<math alttext="2 cm"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Therefore, the area of this rectangle is <math alttext="left parenthesis 4 cm right parenthesis left parenthesis 2 cm right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>)</mo></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="8 cm squared"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum, <math alttext="in cm"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, of the length and width of the rectangle, not the area, <math alttext="in cm squared"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the perimeter, <math alttext="in cm"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, of the rectangle, not the area, <math alttext="in cm squared"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the length and width of the rectangle squared, not the area.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"4420e500","external_id":"76f07394-0a95-4e65-86b8-e42618d65c92","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"096e7ca7-535a-43c1-a773-3edf7dfda31a","uId":"cce9833e-d584-45b2-87ca-c6dc9bd39d92","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>What is the area of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext=\"4 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> and a width of <math alttext=\"2 cm\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"360cb884-e056-4da9-b845-1b2f1b6ae601","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 cm squared\"><mn>6</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"9eea382e-cf7d-42ac-b0a9-bc63f318fb27","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8 cm squared\"><mn>8</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"ffb279aa-4624-4600-97e3-111747624f24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12 cm squared\"><mn>12</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"9db1eaef-eb78-4768-b1b5-95d9fd91895f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36 cm squared\"><mn>36</mn>\n<mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msup></math></p>"}],"keys":["9eea382e-cf7d-42ac-b0a9-bc63f318fb27"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The area of a rectangle with length <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> 