<mfrac>\n<mn>135</mn>\n<mn>8</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. It's given that triangles <math alttext=\"italic upper A italic upper B italic upper C\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mtext></math> and <math alttext=\"italic upper D italic upper E italic upper F\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">F</mtext></math> are similar and each side length of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper A italic upper B italic upper C\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mtext></math> is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> times the corresponding side length of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper D italic upper E italic upper F\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">F</mtext></math>. For two similar triangles, if each side length of the first triangle is <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> times the corresponding side length of the second triangle, then the area of the first triangle is <math alttext=\"k squared\"><msup>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math> times the area of the second triangle. Therefore, the area of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper A italic upper B italic upper C\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mtext></math> is <math alttext=\"4 squared\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math>, times the area of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper D italic upper E italic upper F\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">F</mtext></math>. It's given that the area of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper A italic upper B italic upper C\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mtext></math> is <math alttext=\"270\"><mn>270</mn>\n</math> square inches. Let <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> represent the area, in square inches, of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper D italic upper E italic upper F\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">F</mtext></math>. It follows that <math alttext=\"270\"><mn>270</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math> times <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, or <math alttext=\"270 equals 16 a\"><mrow>\n<mn>270</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>16</mn>\n<mi>a</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 270 Over 16 EndFraction equals a\"><mfrac><mn>270</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 135 Over 8 EndFraction equals a\"><mfrac><mn>135</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Thus, the area, in square inches, of triangle <math alttext=\"italic upper D italic upper E italic upper F\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">E</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">F</mtext></math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 135 Over 8 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>135</mn>\n<mn>8</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. Note that 135/8, 16.87, and 16.88 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"9657587b-66c2-4743-91d3-22e3bf8ab94e","correct_answer":["135/8","16.87","16.88"]},"createDate":1691007959837,"updateDate":1691007959837}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959837, 1691007959837),
    ($SATQ$468613c0$SATQ$, $SATQ$ea4fb9f5-47ef-4d74-89e2-5f8e44710904$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext="56"><mn>56</mn>
</math> centimeters and a height of <math alttext="112"><mn>112</mn>
</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ea375224-a6b2-4492-8e29-c6d856dccf40","content":"<p><math alttext=\"168\"><mn>168</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3c2ee567-348a-45a7-81e7-e04a52f0d16b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,136\"><mn>3,136</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"abd9129a-0579-4915-a10b-8f65dd84c7db","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,272\"><mn>6,272</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The area, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals one half b h"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> is the base length and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the triangle. It&rsquo;s given that a triangle has a base length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="56"><mn>56</mn></math> centimeters and a height of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="112"><mn>112</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="56"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="112"><mn>112</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals one half b h"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 3,136"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3,136</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="3,136"><mn>3,136</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="56 plus 112"><mn>56</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>112</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis one fourth right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"468613c0","external_id":"ea4fb9f5-47ef-4d74-89e2-5f8e44710904","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ec3b9eac-b45e-4808-9a85-1f68c0a53bb6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a height of <math alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ea375224-a6b2-4492-8e29-c6d856dccf40","content":"<p><math alttext=\"168\"><mn>168</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3c2ee567-348a-45a7-81e7-e04a52f0d16b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,136\"><mn>3,136</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"abd9129a-0579-4915-a10b-8f65dd84c7db","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,272\"><mn>6,272</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the base length and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the triangle. It&rsquo;s given that a triangle has a base length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> centimeters and a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 3,136\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3,136</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3,136\"><mn>3,136</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56 plus 112\"><mn>56</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>112</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one fourth right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017725,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"468613c0","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1755117017725,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"ea4fb9f5-47ef-4d74-89e2-5f8e44710904","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"ec3b9eac-b45e-4808-9a85-1f68c0a53bb6","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a height of <math alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>","keys":["7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"ea375224-a6b2-4492-8e29-c6d856dccf40","content":"<p><math alttext=\"168\"><mn>168</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3c2ee567-348a-45a7-81e7-e04a52f0d16b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7fc77ffe-8c89-46ee-9b8c-34d1198054e2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,136\"><mn>3,136</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"abd9129a-0579-4915-a10b-8f65dd84c7db","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6,272\"><mn>6,272</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the base length and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the triangle. It&rsquo;s given that a triangle has a base length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> centimeters and a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"112\"><mn>112</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 3,136\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3,136</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3,136\"><mn>3,136</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56 plus 112\"><mn>56</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>112</mn></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one fourth right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 112 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>112</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","externalid":"ea4fb9f5-47ef-4d74-89e2-5f8e44710904","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1755117017725,"updateDate":1755117017725}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017725, 1755117017725),
