</math> lies on <math alttext="line segment upper Y upper Z"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> such that <math alttext="line segment upper P upper Q"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to&nbsp;<math alttext="line segment upper X upper Y"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If the measure of angle&nbsp;<math alttext="upper X upper Z upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext="63 degree"><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext="upper X upper P upper Q"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["153"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["153"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="153"><mn>153</mn>
</math>. Since it's given that <math alttext="line segment upper P upper Q"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext="line segment upper X upper Y"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> and angle <math alttext="upper Y"><mi>Y</mi>
</math> is a right angle, angle <math alttext="upper Z upper Q upper P"><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is also a right angle. Angle <math alttext="upper Z upper P upper Q"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is complementary to angle <math alttext="upper X upper Z upper Y"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math>, which means its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext="90 minus 63"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, or <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math>. Since angle <math alttext="upper X upper P upper Q"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is supplementary to angle <math alttext="upper Z upper P upper Q"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext="180 minus 27"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or <math alttext="153"><mn>153</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"48fb6483","external_id":"c7393c8f-4256-438b-bd7c-1da38024e64c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"99b4ba53-8162-4ccb-aeda-30022450d018","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, point <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, and point <math alttext=\"upper Q\"><mi>Q</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> such that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If the measure of angle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"63 degree\"><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["153"],"correct_answer":["153"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>. Since it's given that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper Q upper P\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is also a right angle. Angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is complementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math>, which means its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"90 minus 63\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. Since angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is supplementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"180 minus 27\"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554986,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"48fb6483","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1743430554986,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"c7393c8f-4256-438b-bd7c-1da38024e64c","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"99b4ba53-8162-4ccb-aeda-30022450d018","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, point <math alttext=\"upper P\"><mi>P</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, and point <math alttext=\"upper Q\"><mi>Q</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper Y upper Z\"><mover><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> such that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>. If the measure of angle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"63 degree\"><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, what is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>?</p>","keys":["153"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>. Since it's given that <math alttext=\"line segment upper P upper Q\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext=\"line segment upper X upper Y\"><mover><mrow><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math> is a right angle, angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper Q upper P\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is also a right angle. Angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is complementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Z upper Y\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Z</mi><mi>Y</mi></math>, which means its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"90 minus 63\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>63</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math>. Since angle <math alttext=\"upper X upper P upper Q\"><mi>X</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is supplementary to angle <math alttext=\"upper Z upper P upper Q\"><mi>Z</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, its measure, in degrees, is <math alttext=\"180 minus 27\"><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"153\"><mn>153</mn>\n</math>.</p>","externalid":"c7393c8f-4256-438b-bd7c-1da38024e64c","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["153"]},"createDate":1743430554986,"updateDate":1743430554986}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554986, 1743430554986),
    ($SATQ$498d6795$SATQ$, $SATQ$ccc97dea-b103-4868-86e4-80b756cd63d7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Right triangles and trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">In triangle <math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mi>B</mi>
	<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, angle <math alttext="upper B"><mi>B</mi>
</math> is a right angle. The length of side <math alttext="upper A upper B"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mi>B</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot"><mrow>
	<mn>10</mn>
	<msqrt>
		<mn>37</mn>
	</msqrt>
</mrow>
</math> and the length of side <math alttext="upper B upper C"><mrow>
	<mi>B</mi>
	<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot"><mrow>
	<mn>24</mn>
	<msqrt>
		<mn>37</mn>
	</msqrt>
</mrow>
</math>. What is the length of side <math alttext="upper A upper C"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"812e2acd-c3af-4198-9e99-ce5e0f01389e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"14 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>14</mn>\n\t<msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>37</mn>\n\t</msqrt>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"73ae6be2-a7ea-49a2-b297-5a2bf838f723","content":"<p><math alttext=\"26 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>26</mn>\n\t<msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>37</mn>\n\t</msqrt>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"29f6e7e1-fd54-4e1b-b8f9-c1c8416c260f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"34 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>34</mn>\n\t<msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>37</mn>\n\t</msqrt>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"122f708b-1dd4-4a5d-805a-380ead940c33","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartRoot 34 dot 37 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>34</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mrow><mn>37</mn></mrow></msqrt></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["73ae6be2-a7ea-49a2-b297-5a2bf838f723"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The Pythagorean theorem states that for a right triangle, <math alttext="c squared equals a squared plus b squared"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> represents the length of the hypotenuse and <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> represent the lengths of the legs. It&rsquo;s given that in triangle <math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, angle <math alttext="upper B"><mi>B</mi>
</math> is a right angle. Therefore, triangle <math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is a right triangle, where the hypotenuse is side <math alttext="upper A upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and the legs are sides <math alttext="upper A upper B"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math alttext="upper B upper C"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the lengths of sides <math alttext="upper A upper B"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math alttext="upper B upper C"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> are <math alttext="10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot"><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext="24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot"><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>, respectively. Substituting these values for <math alttext="a"><mi>a</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="b"><mi>b</mi>
</math> in the formula <math alttext="c squared equals a squared plus b squared"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;yields <math alttext="c squared equals left parenthesis 10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis 24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squared"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="c squared equals 100 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis plus 576 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>576</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="c squared equals 676 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>676</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="c equals plus or minus 26 StartRoot 37 EndRoot"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>26</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>. Since <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> represents the length of the hypotenuse, side&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
