</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;yields <math alttext=\"c squared equals left parenthesis 10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis 24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squared\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"c squared equals 100 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis plus 576 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>576</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"c squared equals 676 left parenthesis 37 right parenthesis\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>676</mn><mfenced><mn>37</mn></mfenced></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"c equals plus or minus 26 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>26</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>. Since <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> represents the length of the hypotenuse, side&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> must be positive. Therefore, the length of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"26 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mn>26</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the result of solving the equation <math alttext=\"c equals 24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot minus 10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>37</mn></msqrt></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"c squared equals left parenthesis 10 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis 24 StartRoot 37 EndRoot right parenthesis squa