> square inches and the area of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn></math> square inches. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k squared equals StartFraction 648 Over 72 EndFraction\"><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>648</mn><mn>72</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k squared equals 9\"><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Taking the square root of each side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals StartRoot 9 EndRoot\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>9</mn></msqrt></math>,&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 3\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. It follows that the length of each side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> times the length of the corresponding side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the length of the longest side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> inches. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> inches is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> times the length of the longest side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>, and the longest side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math> is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 36 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn></math>, inches.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of the longest side of a rectangle with side lengths that are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one ninth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math> the corresponding side lengths of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>, rather than a rectangle with an area that is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one ninth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math> the area of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the factor by which the area of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is larger than the area of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>, not the length, in inches, of the longest side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of the longest side of rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>, not rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper E upper F upper G upper H\"><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>H</mi></math>.</p>","externalid":"a5e0e74e-362f-4f21-aade-6a5d1b2518e0","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1755117017721,"updateDate":1755117017721}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017721, 1755117017721),
    ($SATQ$50774285$SATQ$, $SATQ$786b1f64-6764-44c0-a7d6-75880720fc77$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math alttext="19"><mn>19</mn>
</math> inches and a width of <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> inches. The prism has a volume of <math alttext="2,736"><mn>2,736</mn>
</math> cubic inches. What is the height, in inches, of the prism?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f17520bd-7d4c-4305-b842-dadba90c3010","content":"<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cfca4c83-4060-4ddf-8472-445853bdd27d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"144\"><mn>144</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7351d285-7178-4fe5-811d-f7e2939bd733","content":"<p><math alttext=\"152\"><mn>152</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. The volume, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a rectangular prism is given by the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals script l w h"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> is the length of the base, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math> is the width of the base, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the prism. It&rsquo;s given that each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> inches and a width of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> inches, and that the prism has a volume of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2,736"><mn>2,736</mn></math> cubic inches. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="19"><mn>19</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2,736"><mn>2,736</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V"><mi>V</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper V equals script l w h"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math> gives <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2,736 equals left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis h right parenthesis"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2,736 equals 152 h"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>152</mn><mi>h</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="152"><mn>152</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="18 equals h"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>. Therefore, the height, in inches, of the prism is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="18"><mn>18</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the area, in square inches, of the base of the prism, not the height, in inches, of the prism.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"50774285","external_id":"786b1f64-6764-44c0-a7d6-75880720fc77","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"a2584b24-45ea-45c8-a114-ea1d12c1275d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> inches. The prism has a volume of <math alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn>\n</math> cubic inches. What is the height, in inches, of the prism?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f17520bd-7d4c-4305-b842-dadba90c3010","content":"<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cfca4c83-4060-4ddf-8472-445853bdd27d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"144\"><mn>144</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7351d285-7178-4fe5-811d-f7e2939bd733","content":"<p><math alttext=\"152\"><mn>152</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a rectangular prism is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals script l w h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> is the length of the base, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> is the width of the base, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the prism. It&rsquo;s given that each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn></math> inches and a width of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> inches, and that the prism has a volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn></math> cubic inches. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals script l w h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736 equals left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis h right parenthesis\"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736 equals 152 h\"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>152</mn><mi>h</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"152\"><mn>152</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18 equals h\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>. Therefore, the height, in inches, of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the area, in square inches, of the base of the prism, not the height, in inches, of the prism.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017719,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"50774285","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1755117017719,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"786b1f64-6764-44c0-a7d6-75880720fc77","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"a2584b24-45ea-45c8-a114-ea1d12c1275d","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> inches. The prism has a volume of <math alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn>\n</math> cubic inches. What is the height, in inches, of the prism?</p>","keys":["81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"81ef216a-af26-4874-8e9e-94e172c4a934","content":"<p><math alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f17520bd-7d4c-4305-b842-dadba90c3010","content":"<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cfca4c83-4060-4ddf-8472-445853bdd27d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"144\"><mn>144</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7351d285-7178-4fe5-811d-f7e2939bd733","content":"<p><math alttext=\"152\"><mn>152</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a rectangular prism is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals script l w h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> is the length of the base, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> is the width of the base, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the prism. It&rsquo;s given that each base of a right rectangular prism has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn></math> inches and a width of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> inches, and that the prism has a volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn></math> cubic inches. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19\"><mn>19</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736\"><mn>2,736</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals script l w h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736 equals left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis h right parenthesis\"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,736 equals 152 h\"><mn>2,736</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>152</mn><mi>h</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"152\"><mn>152</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18 equals h\"><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>. Therefore, the height, in inches, of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18\"><mn>18</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the area, in square inches, of the base of the prism, not the height, in inches, of the prism.</p>","externalid":"786b1f64-6764-44c0-a7d6-75880720fc77","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1755117017719,"updateDate":1755117017719}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017719, 1755117017719),
