 description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled t, m, and n.</li>\n<li>Line t intersects both line m and line n.</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line t and line m, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:\n<ul>\n<li>Bottom left: 170°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line t and line n, 1 angle is labeled clockwise from top left as follows:\n<ul>\n<li>Bottom left: w°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, line <math alttext=\"m\"><mi>m</mi>\n</math> is parallel to line <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"7bf2c7eb-d2eb-49db-a4cf-7cd376347a2c","templateid":"71e054d5-f702-4974-aa43-fa6f0278a11c","vaultid":"68804e55-4287-4ca9-b270-5e8d96e44f0c","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"5d1d94f0-c173-49d1-bbb8-2ad8f73418c9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b7769503-5522-44aa-9831-1410fd40882b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"30\"><mn>30</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"263dec7b-f0a4-4092-9413-9e9950430bc0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"879b421a-bb1d-4977-aded-009147281ed7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"170\"><mn>170</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1691007959839,"updateDate":1691007959839}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959839, 1691007959839),
    ($SATQ$5252e606$SATQ$, $SATQ$21b61a47-8395-41b7-9031-ab756ca63c22$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$33b61eda-6145-4f1c-be92-6aa4ff5c86e7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The side length of a square is <math alttext="55 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis"><mrow><mn>55</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math>. What is the area, <math alttext="in cm squared"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the square?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d59b3137-f4e7-426f-9468-c6f456262f24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"110\"><mn>110</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e19f7357-ebdc-4d4f-8fa5-cb2f7ab824cf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"220\"><mn>220</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"65182a88-0977-4c86-bdb5-39d09099f2c8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,025\"><mn>3,025</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"46aa47a2-8413-4d6c-99ac-5fe28a31c755","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12,100\"><mn>12,100</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["65182a88-0977-4c86-bdb5-39d09099f2c8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The area <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="in square centimeters left parenthesis cm squared right parenthesis"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math>, of a square with side length <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math>, <math alttext="in cm"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, is given by the formula <math alttext="upper A equals s squared"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<msup>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that the square has a side length of <math alttext="55 cm"><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. Substituting <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="s"><mi>s</mi>
</math> in the formula <math alttext="upper A equals s squared"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<msup>
		<mi>s</mi>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="upper A equals 55 squared"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>55</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext="upper A equals 3,025"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>3,025</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the area, <math alttext="in cm squared"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the square is <math alttext="3,025"><mn>3,025</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the perimeter, <math alttext="in cm"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, of the square, not its area, <math alttext="in cm squared"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"5252e606","external_id":"21b61a47-8395-41b7-9031-ab756ca63c22","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"33b61eda-6145-4f1c-be92-6aa4ff5c86e7","uId":"0e07dfe3-a42f-41e8-ae86-7ad9a2b6352c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The side length of a square is <math alttext=\"55 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>55</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math>. What is the area, <math alttext=\"in cm squared\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the square?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d59b3137-f4e7-426f-9468-c6f456262f24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"110\"><mn>110</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e19f7357-ebdc-4d4f-8fa5-cb2f7ab824cf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"220\"><mn>220</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"65182a88-0977-4c86-bdb5-39d09099f2c8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3,025\"><mn>3,025</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"46aa47a2-8413-4d6c-99ac-5fe28a31c755","content":"<p><math alttext=\"12,100\"><mn>12,100</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["65182a88-0977-4c86-bdb5-39d09099f2c8"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"in square centimeters left parenthesis cm squared right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math>, of a square with sid