t follows that the length of side <math alttext=\"upper M upper O\"><mrow>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mi>O</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is half the length of hypotenuse <math alttext=\"upper A upper O\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>O</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, and the length of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper M\"><mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>M</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"StartRoot 3 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> times the length of side <math alttext=\"upper M upper O\"><mrow>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mi>O</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"upper A upper O equals w StartRoot 3 EndRoot\"><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> cm. Therefore, <math alttext=\"upper M upper O equals StartFraction w StartRoot 3 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>M</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> cm and <math alttext=\"upper A upper M equals StartFraction w StartRoot 3 EndRoot StartRoot 3 EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> cm, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"upper A upper M equals StartFraction 3 w Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> cm. Since <math alttext=\"upper A upper M equals 142\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mi>M</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>142</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> cm, it follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 3 w Over 2 EndFraction equals 142\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>142</mn></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"3 w equals 284\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>3</mn>\n<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>284</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"w equals StartFraction 284 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mi>w</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>284</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>.&nbsp;Note that 284/3, 94.66, and 94.67 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"081f3aa6-88ed-4da7-bc3a-e7bbfa7b4fca","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["284/3","94.66","94.67"]},"createDate":1743430554979,"updateDate":1743430554979}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554979, 1743430554979)
